  <event id="184">
      <start>16:30</start>
      <duration>01:00</duration>
      <room>H.1308</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Common package and patch management for SUSE Linux</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>openSUSE</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Zypp - SUSE package management&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Zypp is the integration of SUSE&amp;#39;s yast2 Package manager and Ximian&amp;#39;s libredcarpet. At Novell we used two solutions so far - Red Carpet and YaST &#xA;package manager - and decided to merge both in a best of breed approach. Zypp features brings SUSE package management technology to a world of new &#xA;possibilities like runtime dependencies on hardware, patterns, full-featured patches and Zenworks integration for a easy enterprise upgrade path.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this talk this technologies will be presented among the current integration of them into the products, the problems faced during the transition and the current roadmap for the future releases.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1841">Duncan Mac-Vicar Prett</person>
      </persons>
